IMPORT prelude

-- Environmental Public Health Act 1987 (Singapore) -- public cleansing offences: littering and spitting (s 17), the presumptions for
-- litter from residential flats (s 17A), dropping substances from vehicles (s 19), illegal dumping (s 20), penalties (s 21) and
-- corrective work orders (ss 21A to 21C).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/EPHA1987.txt (amendments to
-- Act 5 of 2023, in force 1 July 2023).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 14 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to Part 3 public cleansing offences.
-- Not encoded: refuse collection, industrial waste and waste collector licensing (Part 3A), pneumatic waste systems (Part 3B), food
-- establishments and hawkers (Part 4), nuisances, burial, and the remaining Parts.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Environmental Public Health Act 1987 -- littering`

§§ `17 -- littering and spitting`

-- s 17(1): no one may (a) deposit or throw any article in a public place except in a dustbin; (b) leave anything where it or its
-- particles will pass into a public place; (c) dry food or anything else in a public place; (d) spill offensive liquid into one;
-- (e) shake out ash, hair, feathers and the like so the wind carries it there; (f) leave behind bottles, cans, food wrappers or food;
-- (g) "spit any substance or expel mucus from the nose" onto a street or public place; (h) abandon a deregistered vehicle,
-- furniture or any bulky article. (2): nothing into a drain, river, reservoir or the sea.
-- (4), (5), (6): a vehicle owner, or a flat owner or occupier, must identify the driver, passengers or occupiers within 14 days;
-- (7) self-incrimination is no excuse.
DECLARE Act IS ONE OF
    `dropping a cigarette butt on the pavement`
    `spitting on the street`
    `drying laundry over a public walkway`
    `leaving an old sofa at the void deck`
    `throwing a bottle into a canal`
    `putting rubbish in a litter bin`

GIVEN `the act` IS AN Act
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the act is a section 17 offence` IF
    CONSIDER `the act`
    WHEN `putting rubbish in a litter bin` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `17A -- litter from a residential flat`

-- s 17A(1)-(4): where litter, spillage, wind-blown debris or spit is proved to have come from a residential flat, it is PRESUMED to
-- have come from (a) every TENANT, if the whole flat was leased, or (b) otherwise every OWNER. (5): rebutted by proving that someone
-- else did it, that the presumed offender was not present, or that they identified the person they reasonably believe did it within
-- 14 DAYS of being asked. (6): only for contraventions from 1 July 2023.
DECLARE Flat HAS
    `the whole flat was leased` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is a tenant` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is an owner` IS A BOOLEAN
    `proved someone else did it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `was not present at the time` IS A BOOLEAN
    `named the likely offender within 14 days` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the flat` IS A Flat
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is presumed to be the litterer` IF
        (IF `the flat`'s `the whole flat was leased` THEN `the flat`'s `the person is a tenant` ELSE `the flat`'s `the person is an owner`)
    AND (NOT `the flat`'s `proved someone else did it`)
    AND (NOT `the flat`'s `was not present at the time`)
    AND (NOT `the flat`'s `named the likely offender within 14 days`)

§§ `19, 20 -- vehicles and dumping`

-- s 19(3)(a): where matter is dropped or spilled from a vehicle, the DRIVER is deemed to have committed the offence unless someone else
-- did it and that person's identity "can be established".
-- s 20(1): dumping refuse from, or using, a vehicle for dumping in a public place. (5), (6): the vehicle may be seized and the court
-- "is to" order forfeiture on proof of use, "even though no person may have been convicted". (8): if there is no prosecution, the
-- vehicle is forfeited 3 months after seizure unless claimed.
GIVEN `prosecuted` IS A BOOLEAN, `months since seizure` IS A NUMBER, `claimed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the seized vehicle is forfeited without a court order` IF
    (NOT `prosecuted`) AND (NOT `claimed`) AND `months since seizure` AT LEAST 3

§§ `21 -- penalties`

-- s 21(1)(a): illegal dumping -- up to $50,000 or 12 months; on a second or later conviction, up to $100,000 AND a MANDATORY prison
-- term of 1 to 12 months. (b): abandoning a bulky article -- $5,000; then $10,000 or 3 months. (c): other offences under ss 17 to 19 --
-- $2,000, then $4,000, then $10,000.
-- (8): the cost of cleaning may be recovered from the offender, or from the employer if committed in the course of employment.
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `illegal dumping`
    `abandoning a bulky article`
    `littering`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence, `previous convictions` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `illegal dumping` THEN (IF `previous convictions` AT LEAST 1 THEN 100000 ELSE 50000)
    WHEN `abandoning a bulky article` THEN (IF `previous convictions` AT LEAST 1 THEN 10000 ELSE 5000)
    OTHERWISE (IF `previous convictions` AT LEAST 2 THEN 10000 ELSE IF `previous convictions` EQUALS 1 THEN 4000 ELSE 2000)

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence, `previous convictions` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the minimum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    IF `the offence` EQUALS `illegal dumping` AND `previous convictions` AT LEAST 1 THEN 1 ELSE 0

§§ `21A to 21C -- corrective work orders`

-- s 21A(1): on conviction under s 17 or 19 of a person aged 16 or over, the court "is to", "unless it has special reasons for not so
-- doing", make a corrective work order of unpaid cleaning work if satisfied it is expedient. (2): not more than 12 HOURS in aggregate.
-- s 21B(2): within 12 months; (3) not more than 3 hours a day. s 21C(2): breach without reasonable excuse -- $5,000 or 2 months.
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence, `age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a corrective work order is available` IF
    `age` AT LEAST 16 AND (NOT `the offence` EQUALS `illegal dumping`)

GIVEN `hours ordered` IS A NUMBER, `hours in a day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the corrective work order is within the limits` IF
    `hours ordered` AT MOST 12 AND `hours in a day` AT MOST 3
